      "note": "Count distinct active medicines in the listed classes, including lithium, antipsychotics, antidepressants, anxiolytics, hypnotics and ADHD medicines. Count oral valproate salts and brands as one medicine. Count each of flupentixol and fluphenazine once across its base and decanoate forms. A maintenance depot counts for its documented treatment interval. A one-off procedural, sedative or antiemetic injection such as midazolam or droperidol does not establish continuing psychiatric treatment. Check the form and use when a brand has more than one presentation."
    }
  ],
  "rule_for_models": "At ages 6 to 17 inclusive, flag four or more distinct group A medicines with overlapping psychiatric use for more than three continuous calendar months, citing the supplies and any evidence of psychiatric use needed for the count, including the directions. Work out shared coverage from supply dates, quantities and directed daily use or documented depot intervals, restarting after a documented interruption and reporting no finding if age, count or duration falls outside the criterion or excluding medicines used only for another purpose leaves fewer than four. If treatment could qualify but age, a necessary indication or continuity is unclear, report only a possible finding and ask for age during treatment, why the named medicine was taken or which medicines were taken together and for how long, leaving borderline gaps, unclear directions and intermittent use for the pharmacist to judge.",
  "cannot_be_seen": "Dispensing does not establish actual use, indication or a prescriber’s intent. Treatment and assessments elsewhere may be missing.",
  "ask_the_gp": "Could you review the ongoing need, safety and monitoring of four or more concurrent psychotropic medicines in this young person?",
  "urgency": "routine",
  "draft": true,
  "signed_by_clinical_reviewer": null,
  "needs_facts": [
    {
      "kind": "observation",
      "what": "Psychiatric indication",
      "meets": "When the count depends on a medicine with several uses, what was it taken for during the shared period? Examples include carbamazepine, lamotrigine, sodium valproate or valproic acid, clobazam, clonazepam and melatonin. Count a medicine only when its psychiatric use is documented for the shared period. Exclude a medicine taken only for another purpose. A general Yes or No that names neither the medicine nor the treatment period cannot settle its use. If that medicine could change the count, keep the finding possible."
    }
  ]
}
